      {
        "id": 46303,
        "name": "plasticbrain",
        "username": "plasticbrain",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/plasticbrain/{size}/2658_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-12-02T10:37:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>major overhaul coming.</p><p>did some playtesting and she was too weak... made some changes... did some playtesting and she was too strong... i've made some more changes and i think i've got her where she needs to be... but i want to playtest her some more before i post the \"final\" version.</p><p>what started out as a off-the-cuff idea for the contest has turned into a real challenge to myself to create a solid playable Villain, one&nbsp; that's difficult to beat but can be defeated by a good hero team playing well. also, balancing in her alternate win condition so it's a realistic threat but not overwhelming is really tough too.</p><p><strong>EDIT 12/4/12: </strong>check out full card version with full ART ready to PnP!!! version 5 in original post above. some notes on playing the deck: be careful of the order in which cards enter the Villain trash. a one-shot shouldn't be put into to the trash until its effects are complete. so if a card tells you to play the top card of the Villain deck, you'll play that next card, and if it's a one-shot too, it'll go into the trash BEFORE the card that told you to play it.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:19:48.401Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
